On successful commit where all flushed manifests are in the committed set, `anyDeleted` is false and `flushedManifests` is never cleared. This is benign since the accumulator isn't reused after commit, but it's inconsistent with `SnapshotProducer.deleteUncommitted()` which always clears when asked. Simpler to always clear:

```java
void deleteUncommitted(Set<ManifestFile> committed, Consumer<String> deleteFunc) {
    for (ManifestFile manifest : flushedManifests) {
        if (!committed.contains(manifest)) {
            deleteFunc.accept(manifest.path());
        }
    }
    flushedManifests.clear();
}
```

